 "notes": {
  "tabs": "Foundry right tabs (Form_EquipSubliming): order forge, identify, ascend, recast, reforge, each 0.125 U high, stacked down from y0=0.0328 U with no gap. The game hides tabs (Lua Form_EquipSubliming.OnActive): forge+identify need the Foundry function, ascend its function, recast and reforge only while the gem function is NOT unlocked; a hidden tab frees its slot (the layout group packs the visible ones from the top). Position of the k-th visible tab = foundry.tab.forge shifted down by k*0.125 U.",
  "grid": "InfinityGrid: columns = grids[..].cols, column pitch = list width / cols, row pitch = lineSize / 640 U (the game reports the exact value at run time: InfinityGrid.LineSize / m_finalLineSize / m_fitScale, layout \"field\" offsets). The scroll position is read from the game; row 1 starts at the list top + padding[1]*(-1) at scroll 0 for a negative top padding (assumed, not yet checked live). The cell template (ascend.cell) is 0.125 x 0.1625 U (80 x 104 units, sits centred in its column slot and its line); the item picture square (ascend.cellIcon) is 0.125 U, 0.0188 U (12 units) below the cell top, the stat bar hangs under it.",
  "card": "Inventory item card: the card fills the left layout and its bottom button row (c_Button) is the last child under a flexible attribute scroll, so inventory.cardLeft / cardRight sit on the card bottom whatever the number of attribute rows. A worn item shows both buttons (Gems / Remove); an item that is not worn only the left one, centred: inventory.cardSolo. inventory.listView = the equipment list viewport, inventory.scrollbar = its scroll bar (the track runs the whole height).",
  "gem": "Gem screen: gem.list = the function list viewport (a one-column grid, gem.cell = a row), the rows follow the config order (Recast 7, Advanced Recast 8, Refine 5, Advanced Refine 6, Gem 1, 11, 2, 3, 4; locked functions drop out) - src/GemRows in the app. gem.button = «Улучшить» of the recast widget.",
  "state": "Rects are for the layout the prefab gives with every authored child active, except: inventory = normal (not bulk) state with the Gem and Foundry buttons shown; hero = gear tab with Foundry/Gem/Switching shown. Hidden buttons shift the others.",
  "cross-check": "Canvas height 640 = U (CanvasScaler reference 1136x640). Verified: inventory list top 0.1906 U vs SellGeometry.Inventory ViewTop 0.190; inventory row LineSize 118 = 0.1844 U vs PitchY 0.1846; hero slot 0 centre -0.3547 U from the centre vs HintGeometry.SlotLeftDx -0.356, y +0.0453 vs +0.0473; left menu 2nd tab centre y 0.305 U (inside 0.2426..0.3676) vs LocatePilot EquipTab click 0.315 U."
 }
